    "https://careers.sru.edu/postings/11041": {
      "title": "Management Technician | Transfer Admissions",
      "description": "Slippery Rock University | Management Technician | Transfer Admissions Skip to Main Content STUDENTS FACULTY AND STAFF ADMINISTRATION ALUMNI, FRIENDS, GIVING PARENTS ADMISSIONS ACADEMICS CAMPUS LIFE ATHLETICS ABOUT SRU NEWS and INFO Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About SRU Human Resources Diversity and Equal Opportunity Benefits Directions Visitors and Community Management Technician | Transfer Admissions Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please provide three professional references in the application form. Posting Details Position Details Posting Number N01243 Classification Title Management Technician Working Title Management Technician | Transfer Admissions Employee Group Staff Bargaining Unit AFSCME Location Main Campus Department Graduate Admissions Pay Rate $46,827 Employment Type Regular FT Work Schedule 8:00 – 4:30 M-F Position Summary Information Position Summary This position coordinates the technical and clerical operations of the transfer articulation system, including Degree Works and Banner Transfer, to support accurate and efficient transfer credit evaluations. Responsibilities include maintaining institutional reference tables, grading tables, course equivalencies, and transfer institution codes, as well as troubleshooting system errors and collaborating with Information Technology, Academic Records and Registration, and other universities to resolve issues and improve system functionality. The position plays an important role in reviewing transcripts and academic policies to determine transfer and military credit applicability, general education waivers, Foundations of Academic Discovery requirements, scholarship eligibility, and appropriate tuition rates based on residency and GPA credentials. Additional duties include processing Advanced Standing and College in High School credits, maintaining student tracking records, coordinating student communications for advising/registration preparation, finalizing admissions records for enrolled students, and resolving incomplete applicant files. Through collaboration with Enrollment Management colleagues and campus partners, this position also contributes to improved processes, responsive customer service, and the university’s enrollment goals while providing admissions application processing, phone coverage, and general office support as needed. Minimum Qualifications Three years of advanced clerical or para-professional work which included the collection, recording, compilation, and presentation of office management or program related information, or any equivalent combination of experience and training. An Associate’s Degree may be substituted for two years of required experience. Successful performance in an interview. Preferred Qualifications Preferred Bachelor’s Degree. Experience in a higher education admissions office. Experience with robust student information systems (Banner especially) and CRMs. Experience working with diverse populations. Posting Detail Information Posting Date 10/28/2026 Closing Date 11/11/2026 Open Until Filled No Notice of Non-Discrimination Slippery Rock University of Pennsylvania does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, gender, sexual orientation, national origin, religion, age, disability, age/or veteran status in its programs or activities in accordance with Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, and other applicable statutes and University policies. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Executive Director- Campus Climate, Culture, and Compliance 208 Old Main Building 104 Maltby Avenue Slippery Rock University Slippery Rock, PA 16057 724.738.2009 Respect for Individuals in the Community Slippery Rock University provides an environment that respects, encourages, and promotes the talents and contributions of all. Slippery Rock University values a community with a shared sense of purpose, where people demonstrate mutual respect and appreciation. Slippery Rock University values diversity that honors and includes all persons regardless of age, creed, disability, ethnic heritage, gender, gender identity, race, religion, sexual orientation, or socioeconomic status in academic and extracurricular endeavor, in the working environment, and in the daily life of the university community. Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide three professional references in the application form. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Optional Documents ADMISSIONS Undergraduate Graduate International Financial Aid/Costs Orientation Visit ACADEMICS Majors and Minors Graduate Programs Academic Departments Colleges Library Academic Services CAMPUS LIFE Living on campus Dining Bookstore Wellness Volunteering Get Involved SPORTS Intercollegiate Athletics Intramural Sports Club Sports Recreation Center Sports Information Rock Athletic Club ABOUT SRU University Profile Accountability Extended Learning Community Employment Arts and Culture NEWS & INFO News Releases Events, Tickets, Calendars Directories Campus Map top of the rock rockpride online Copyright Slippery Rock University of Pennsy