tiple certification areas. Additionally, some temporary faculty may be hired to teach coursework in the CIEL Department as needed. Minimum Qualifications Masters in Education or related field. Successful and recent teaching and/or administrative experience in Birth-12th grade programs or in higher education teacher preparation. Ability to articulate knowledge and understanding of current best practices in supervision or a content-related field in PK-12 education. Commitment to the education of diverse populations. Successful performance in an interview and teaching demonstration. Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching and/or supervision experience in higher education strongly preferred. Posting Detail Information Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Respect for Individuals in the Community Slippery Rock University provides an environment that respects, encourages, and promotes the talents and contributions of all. Slippery Rock University values a community with a shared sense of purpose, where people demonstrate mutual respect and appreciation. Slippery Rock University values diversity that honors and includes all persons regardless of age, creed, disability, ethnic heritage, gender, gender identity, race, religion, sexual orientation, or socioeconomic status in academic and extracurricular endeavor, in the working environment, and in the daily life of the university community. Notice of Non-Discrimination Slippery Rock University of Pennsylvania does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, religion, age, disability, or veteran status in its programs or activities in accordance with Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, and other applicable statutes and University policies. The following person has been designated to handle i