      "title": "Special Education | Assistant Professor Tenure Track August 2027| I02514",
      "description": "Slippery Rock University | Special Education | Assistant Professor Tenure Track August 2027| I02514 Skip to Main Content STUDENTS FACULTY AND STAFF ADMINISTRATION ALUMNI, FRIENDS, GIVING PARENTS ADMISSIONS ACADEMICS CAMPUS LIFE ATHLETICS ABOUT SRU NEWS and INFO Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About SRU Human Resources Diversity and Equal Opportunity Benefits Directions Visitors and Community Special Education | Assistant Professor Tenure Track August 2027| I02514 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Graduate and undergraduate transcripts are required for this position. Applicants may upload either official or unofficial transcripts using the \"Transcript\" selection under Required Documents Official transcripts are required prior to appointment. The recommended candidate will be required to complete criminal background check, including Act 34 Background Check and Act 151 (Child Abuse) Background Check and Federal Criminal (FBI) clearance prior to appointment. The recommended candidate will also be required to submit a completed Act 24 form (PDE-6004) prior to employment. Full consideration will be given to applications received by December 2nd, 2026. Posting Details Position Details Posting Number I02514 Classification Title Assistant Professor Working Title Special Education | Assistant Professor Tenure Track August 2027| I02514 Employee Group Faculty Bargaining Unit APSCUF Location Main Campus Department Special Education Pay Rate Employment Type Regular FT Work Schedule This position would have a work schedule that follows the CBA at the minimum. This person will teach 12 credits or four courses during the fall and spring semesters totaling 24 credits. The hours per day will vary depending on his/her schedule. Position Summary Information Position Summary Special Education Department Faculty Member Slippery Rock University invites applications for a full-time Assistant Professor in the Special Education Department beginning August 2027. Responsibilities: The primary role will be teaching assignments in the Special Education undergraduate, graduate and doctoral programs. This position also supports doctoral dissertation committee service, accreditation efforts, assessment, student advisement at all levels, development of community partnerships and expansion of opportunities for student’s within our diverse repertoire of programs. This position requires teaching face to face and within the online setting. It also includes supervision of student teachers and field students and participation in department, College of Education and university-wide committees, local, regional, and national presentations, and peer-reviewed publications. The assignment may include off-campus and/or web based instruction. Minimum Qualifications Doctorate in special education or related field. Certification in special education. Three or more years experience teaching students with disabilities within the K-12 setting.. Evidence of potential for scholarship and research agenda. Evidence of ability to engage undergraduate and/or graduate students in research. Evidence of ability to engage with students through advisement and mentoring Evidence of potential to obtain grant funding for research and/or training activities. *Successful performance in an on-campus interview, and a teaching demonstration are required. Candidates must demonstrate a commitment to the education of diverse populations. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of expertise in systems-level academic and behavioral interventions, including multi-tiered systems of support. Certification in special education supervision. Five or more years experience teaching students with disabilities Experience teaching within a college or university setting in both face to face and online settings. Experience with field supervision and student teaching. Expertise in writing legally defendable IEP’s Experience implementing interventions based upon student need. Experience as an academic student advisor at the college level. Experience as a theses and/ or doctoral dissertation committee member. Posting Detail Information Posting Date Closing Date Open Until Filled No Respect for Individuals in the Community Slippery Rock University provides an environment that respects, encourages, and promotes the talents and contributions of all. Slippery Rock University values a community with a shared sense of purpose, where people demonstrate mutual respect and appreciation. Slippery Rock University values diversity that honors and includes all persons regardless of age, creed, disability, ethnic heritage, gender, gender identity, race, religion, sexual orientation, or socioeconomic status in academic and extracurricular endeavor, in the working environment, and in the daily life of the university community. Notice of Non-Discrimination Slippery Rock University of Pennsylvania does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, religion, age, disability, or veteran status in its programs or activities in accordance with Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, and other applicable statutes and University policies. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Assistant Vice President of Human Resources and Compliance/Title IX Coordinator 008 Old Main Building 104 Maltby Avenue Slippery Rock University Slippery Rock, PA 16057 724.738.2070 Special Instructions to Applicants Graduate and undergraduate transcripts are required for this position. Applicants may upload either official or unofficial transcripts using the “Transcript” selection under Required Documents Official transcripts are required prior to appointment. The recommended candidate will be required to complete criminal background check, including Act 34 Background Check and Act 151 (Child Abuse) Background Check and Federal Criminal ( FBI ) clearance prior to appointment. The recommended candidate will also be required to submit a completed Act 24 form ( PDE -6004) prior to employment. Full consideration will be given to applications received by December 2nd, 2026. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have three years experience teaching special education? YES NO Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Unofficial Transcripts 2 Optional Documents Unofficial Transcripts 3 Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness (e.g. peer reviews, student evaluations, honors and awards, etc.) Portfolio ADMISSIONS Undergraduate Graduate International Financial Aid/Costs Orientation Visit ACADEMICS Majors and Minors Graduate Programs Academic Departments Colleges Library Academic Services CAMPUS LIFE Living on campus Dining Bookstore Wellness Volunteering Get Involved SPORTS Intercollegiate Athletics Intramural Sports Club Sports Recreation Center Sports Information Rock Athletic Club ABOUT SRU University Profile Accountability Extended Learning Community Employment Arts and Culture NEWS & INFO News Releases Events, Tickets, Calendars Directories Campus Map top of the rock rockpride online Copyright Slippery Rock University of Pennsylvania • 1 Morrow Way Slippery Rock, PA 16057 • Webmaster • Right to Know Policy • Sitemap • Login To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://careers.sru.edu/postings/11051": {
      "title": "Biology Assistant Professor | Tenure Track Fall 2027|| I02589",
      "description": "Slippery Rock University | Biology Assistant Professor | Tenure Track Fall 2027|| I02589 Skip to Main Content STUDENTS FACULTY AND STAFF ADMINISTRATION ALUMNI, FRIENDS, GIVING PARENTS ADMISSIONS ACADEMICS CAMPUS LIFE ATHLETICS ABOUT SRU NEWS and INFO Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help About SRU Human Resources Diversity and Equal Opportunity Benefits Directions Visitors and Community Biology Assistant Professor | Tenure Track Fall 2027|| I02589 Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. To email this position to a friend, click on the Email to a Friend link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must electronically submit a teaching philosophy and research plan. These documents should be submitted as part of the online application. The teaching philosophy should be submitted using the \"Teaching Philosophy\" tab and the Research Plan should be submitted using the \"Research Plan\" tab. Please include three professional references with your submitted materials. Graduate and undergraduate transcripts are required for this position. Transcripts must be uploaded using the online system. Official transcripts are required prior to appointment. Recommended candidates will be required to a complete criminal background check, including Act 34 Background Check and Act 151 (Child Abuse) Background Check and Federal Criminal (FBI) clearance prior to appointment. Full consideration will be given to applications received by December 2nd, 2026. Posting Details Position Details Posting Number I02589 Classification Title Biology Assistant Professor | Tenure Track Fall 2027 Working Title Biology Assistant Professor | Tenure Track Fall 2027|| I02589 Employee Group Faculty Bargaining Unit APSCUF Location Main Campus Department Biology Pay Rate Employment Type Regular FT Work Schedule Teaching schedule for the 2027-2028 academic year has not as yet been created though the faculty member will have a 24 contact hour teaching schedule. Position Summary Information Position Summary Slippery Rock University invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor in the Department of Biology beginning August 2027. The faculty member’s primary teaching responsibilities will include various Microbiology and Introductory Majors Biology courses. This individual will also be required to teach introductory and advanced biology major courses, and non-major courses for our general education program, as needed. Additional teaching responsibilities may include courses in an area of specialization. Candidates must exhibit a commitment to excellence in teaching in a Liberal Arts setting, establishment of a productive research program in the candidate’s area of expertise that will involve undergraduates, and membership/contribution to department, college, and university committees. Faculty in the department are expected to engage in ongoing scholarly growth and professional development and to build a strong undergraduate research program that involves actively mentoring students. Slippery Rock University and the Department of Biology offer strong institutional support for teaching and research. The university has many resources for student and faculty scholarship and for teaching microbiology, including a BSL2 facility, a wide range of microscopes including a confocal fluorescence and scanning electron microscope. Moreover, the Department of Biology is research-active, with faculty pursuing diverse interests that create a highly collaborative environment and foster interdisciplinary research. Minimum Qualifications A broadly trained microbiologist with PhD in Biology or related field completed by July 1, 2027. Evidence of professional competence, and ability to work productively with students and colleagues. Commitment to the education of diverse populations. Successful performance in an on-campus interview, including a teaching and a research presentation. Preferred Qualifications Evidence of the ability and or potential to teach undergraduate biology courses effectively Evidence of the ability to teach medical microbiology Evidence of feasible and productive research agenda Evidence of the ability to involve undergraduate students in research Demonstrated commitment to department/ university service Posting Detail Information Posting Date 11/04/2026 Closing Date Open Until Filled Yes Respect for Individuals in the Community Slippery Rock University provides an environment that respects, encourages, and promotes the talents and contributions of all. Slippery Rock University values a community with a shared sense of purpose, where people demonstrate mutual respect and appreciation. Slippery Rock University values diversity that honors and includes all persons regardless of age, creed, disability, ethnic heritage, gender, gender identity, race, religion, sexual orientation, or socioeconomic status in academic and extracurricular endeavor, in the working environment, and in the daily life of the university community. Notice of Non-Discrimination Slippery Rock University of Pennsylvania does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, national origin, religion, age, disability, or veteran status in its programs or activities in accordance with Title IX of the Educational Amendments of 1972, the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, and other applicable statutes and University policies. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding the non-discrimination policies: Human Resources 208 Old Main Building 104 Maltby Avenue Slippery Rock University Slippery Rock, PA 16057 724.738.2070 Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must electronically submit a teaching philosophy and research plan. These documents should be submitted as part of the online application. The teaching philosophy should be submitted using the “Teaching Philosophy” tab and the Research Plan should be submitted using the “Research Plan” tab. Please include three professional references with your submitted materials. Graduate and undergraduate transcripts are required for this position. Transcripts must be uploaded using the online system. Official transcripts are required prior to appointment. Recommended candidates will be required to a complete criminal background check, including Act 34 Background Check and Act 151 (Child Abuse) Background Check and Federal Criminal ( FBI ) clearance prior to appointment. Full consideration will be given to applications received by December 2nd, 2026. Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts Unofficial Transcripts 2 Research Plan Optional Documents Research Philosophy Unofficial Transcripts 3 ADMISSIONS Undergraduate Graduate International Financial Aid/Costs Orientation Visit ACADEMICS Majors and Minors Graduate Programs Academic Departments Colleges Library Academic Services CAMPUS LIFE Living on campus Dining Bookstore Wellness Volunteering Get Involved SPORTS Intercollegiate Athletics Intramural Sports Club Sports Recreation Center Sports Information Rock Athletic Club ABOUT SRU University Profile Accountability Extended Learning Community Employment Arts and Culture NEWS & INFO News Releases Events, Tickets, Calendars Directories Campus Map top of the rock rockpride online Copyright Slippery Rock University of Pennsylvania • 1 Morrow Way Slippery Rock, PA 16057 • Webmaster • Right to Know Policy • Sitemap • Login To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
